      "content": "yeah but its more than just a \"narrative\" though. when people point out things like the control of information or how certain groups manipulate the economy, those are actual facts, not just a \"feeling\". if they are just exposing the truth, why do you frame it like it's just some psychological trick or a way to feel superior? wouldn't it make more sense to say they are uncovering the actual corruption?",
